      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "rates for Section 340B hospitals different from the rates for all other hospitals and purported to base those rates on acquisition costs, but it did not conduct the cost study that the statute requires."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Thomas",
      "case_id": "2021-20-1114",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "04c04c6f4ebb6c86b7acb501f483c54ef28468c8579ab9e7df9aa4d43f0b29a6",
      "evidence_id": "ev-04c04c6f4ebb-0000-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 6,
        "start": 6
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE THOMAS: Mr. Verrilli, if we don't agree with your last statement but rather with the D.C. Circuit that you -- and its application of Chevron and that we agree that Chevron disposes of this, would you argue or are you arguing that we should overrule Chevron to get to the statutory approach that you're taking?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "American Hospital Association (Petitioner)",
      "case_id": "2021-20-1114",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "04c04c6f4ebb6c86b7acb501f483c54ef28468c8579ab9e7df9aa4d43f0b29a6",
      "evidence_id": "ev-04c04c6f4ebb-0000-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 7,
        "start": 7
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "We think this is a situation in which the statute is clear, unambiguous, at the first stage of Chevron I -- of Chevron and, therefore, that one doesn't get to the -- to the question of whether Chevron needs to be overruled."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "American Hospital Association (Petitioner)",
      "case_id": "2021-20-1114",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "04c04c6f4ebb6c86b7acb501f483c54ef28468c8579ab9e7df9aa4d43f0b29a6",
      "evidence_id": "ev-04c04c6f4ebb-0000-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 7,
        "start": 7
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Congress can't possibly have intended to delegate the agency the authority to do that."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "American Hospital Association (Petitioner)",
      "case_id": "2021-20-1114",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "04c04c6f4ebb6c86b7acb501f483c54ef28468c8579ab9e7df9aa4d43f0b29a6",
      "evidence_id": "ev-04c04c6f4ebb-0000-0005",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 9,
        "start": 9
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Congress doesn't just legislate objectives. It legislates the means by which those objectives are to be accomplished."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "American Hospital Association (Petitioner)",
      "case_id": "2021-20-1114",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "04c04c6f4ebb6c86b7acb501f483c54ef28468c8579ab9e7df9aa4d43f0b29a6",
      "evidence_id": "ev-04c04c6f4ebb-0000-0006",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 11,
        "start": 11
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the purpose of the statute is to ensure reliability and accuracy and transparency in the methods that Congress has prescribed for calculating the rates and accuracy and transparency in the calculation of average cost rates by using a cost study, accuracy and transparency in the calculation of price-based rates using the statutory formula, adjusted as necessary for purposes of the paragraph."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioners",
      "case_id": "2021-20-1114",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "04c04c6f4ebb6c86b7acb501f483c54ef28468c8579ab9e7df9aa4d43f0b29a6",
      "evidence_id": "ev-04c04c6f4ebb-0001-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Now, you know, we've gone back and forth in the briefs about whether you can have a major adjustment or a minor adjustment, but I do think, with respect to the meaning of the word \"adjust,\" at a minimum, what it does is require you to have a consistent baseline. You start with A and you adjust A. You don't start with A and substitute something totally different in for it and call it an adjustment. So --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioners",
      "case_id": "2021-20-1114",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "04c04c6f4ebb6c86b7acb501f483c54ef28468c8579ab9e7df9aa4d43f0b29a6",
      "evidence_id": "ev-04c04c6f4ebb-0001-0001",
      "kind": "allegation",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 39,
        "start": 39
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Petitioners ask this Court to hold that Congress compelled Medicare to knowingly and dramatically overpay 340B hospitals for covered drugs at the direct expense of Medicare beneficiaries and other hospitals."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Thomas",
      "case_id": "2021-20-1114",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "04c04c6f4ebb6c86b7acb501f483c54ef28468c8579ab9e7df9aa4d43f0b29a6",
      "evidence_id": "ev-04c04c6f4ebb-0001-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 42,
        "start": 42
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE THOMAS: So how often do you -- have you conducted subclause 1 surveys?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2021-20-1114",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "04c04c6f4ebb6c86b7acb501f483c54ef28468c8579ab9e7df9aa4d43f0b29a6",
      "evidence_id": "ev-04c04c6f4ebb-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 43,
        "start": 43
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: Counsel, what do I do with the fact that 3a, when it's calculating"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
      "case_id": "2021-20-1114",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "04c04c6f4ebb6c86b7acb501f483c54ef28468c8579ab9e7df9aa4d43f0b29a6",
      "evidence_id": "ev-04c04c6f4ebb-0002-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 59,
        "start": 59
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAVANAUGH: But the word \"overpayment\" with respect to 340B hospitals is -- is questionable, isn't it? At least the amicus brief suggests they provide -- they're about a third of the DSH hospitals in the country."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Federation of American Hospitals",
      "case_id": "2021-20-1114",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "04c04c6f4ebb6c86b7acb501f483c54ef28468c8579ab9e7df9aa4d43f0b29a6",
      "evidence_id": "ev-04c04c6f4ebb-0002-0006",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 60,
        "start": 60
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the amicus briefs of the Federation of American Hospitals and the rural hospitals that are filed on our side of the case, and those briefs explain that the rural hospitals in particular"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2021-20-1114",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "04c04c6f4ebb6c86b7acb501f483c54ef28468c8579ab9e7df9aa4d43f0b29a6",
      "evidence_id": "ev-04c04c6f4ebb-0003-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 63,
        "start": 63
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Does the government agree with that statement of when Chevron deference applies?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Michel",
      "case_id": "2021-20-1114",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "04c04c6f4ebb6c86b7acb501f483c54ef28468c8579ab9e7df9aa4d43f0b29a6",
      "evidence_id": "ev-04c04c6f4ebb-0003-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 63,
        "start": 63
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I think that is an accurate statement about Chevron deference."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Federation of American Hospitals",
      "case_id": "2021-20-1114",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "04c04c6f4ebb6c86b7acb501f483c54ef28468c8579ab9e7df9aa4d43f0b29a6",
      "evidence_id": "ev-04c04c6f4ebb-0003-0003",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 75,
        "start": 75
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "And if you read the Federation of American Hospitals' amicus brief, it cites a study indicating that nearly half of 340B hospitals come out ahead under these rules."
    },
